# Cloudflare Pages redirect/rewrite rules.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHY THERE IS NO `/*  /index.html  200` RULE HERE (do not add one)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# That is the classic "SPA fallback" recipe, but on this project it is both
# REDUNDANT and RISKY:
#
# 1. REDUNDANT — Cloudflare Pages already does it for you. From Cloudflare's own
#    docs: "If your project does not include a top-level 404.html file, Pages
#    assumes that you are deploying a single-page application ... and serves the
#    root (/) for any incoming path that does not correspond to a static asset."
#    This repo intentionally ships NO 404.html, so /dashboard, /profile and any
#    other deep link already return 200 with index.html.
#
#    Verified locally with `wrangler pages dev dist`:
#      /                     200
#      /dashboard            200
#      /profile              200
#      /some/random/deep/link 200
#      /index.html           308 -> /
#
# 2. RISKY — the rule loops against Pages' default html handling: the rewrite
#    target /index.html gets `.html`/`/index` stripped, matches /* again, and
#    Cloudflare rejects it:
#      ▲ Infinite loop detected in this rule and has been ignored
#      ✘ Invalid _redirects configuration ... [code: 100324]
#    Locally it is only a warning; the deploy-time API validator can hard-fail
#    the deployment with code 100324.
#
# NOTE: the alternative mechanism, `assets.not_found_handling:
# "single-page-application"` in wrangler.jsonc, is a *Workers static assets*
# setting. Classic Cloudflare Pages REJECTS any `assets` block in the config
# file ("Configuration file for Pages projects does not support \"assets\""),
# so that is not available here either. Native Pages SPA detection is the
# correct mechanism for this deployment.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep this file: it makes dist/_redirects exist, so adding a REAL redirect
# later is a one-liner. Rules are evaluated top to bottom; first match wins.
# Also: never add a 404.html to public/ — that would switch Pages out of SPA
# mode and break every deep link.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Examples (uncomment and adapt) ------------------------------------------
# /docs/*  https://docs.example.com/:splat  301
# /old     /new                              308
# /blog/:slug  /articles/:slug               301
